# sheng: screen-keyboard system defaults (compiled by `glib-compile-schemas`).
#
# preload-view-enabled=true
#   kylin-virtual-keyboard builds its QML view lazily: with this false (the
#   upstream default) virtualkeyboardview.cpp initView() constructs a fresh
#   QQuickView, reloads the QML tree and the theme, and recompiles shaders on
#   EVERY pop, and destroyView() deletes it on hide:
#       if (view_ != nullptr && preloadViewEnabled) return;      // initView
#       if (!isPreloadViewEnabled()) view_.release()->deleteLater();  // destroyView
#   Measured on the sheng tablet: show->visible 0.43/0.53/0.51 s with false vs
#   0.34/0.36/0.32/0.31 s with true (~38% faster, and the "view rebuilt" log
#   lines disappear entirely).  The remaining ~300 ms is kylin-wlcom mapping a
#   ~3048x1220 surface on DSI-1 at scale 2.5 and is not affected by this key.
#
#   KNOWN UPSTREAM DEFECT, WORKED AROUND AT RUNTIME BY sheng-osk-rotate:
#   once the view is reused, its window size freezes at view-creation time.
#   handleScreensChanged() (virtualkeyboardmanager.cpp:274) and
#   updateGeometry() (virtualkeyboardview.cpp:102) both bail out while the
#   keyboard is hidden, and initView() returns early at :150 without ever
#   re-applying the geometry from :196.  So with this key on:
#       * rotate while the keyboard is OPEN   -> it adapts (updateGeometry runs)
#       * hide the keyboard, rotate, reopen   -> it would keep the old width
#   The sheng-osk-rotate daemon (installed by install_osk_tap unless
#   OSK_ROTATE_ENV=0) polls com.kylin.statusmanager.interface.get_current_rotation
#   and, ONLY when the orientation changed while the keyboard was hidden,
#   restarts the keyboard process so the view is rebuilt at the current
#   orientation.  A visible keyboard is never touched.  That is what lets
#   "boots and pops fast" and "hide, rotate, reopen follows the screen" hold at
#   the same time without recompiling the keyboard.
#
#   The upstream-grade one-line fix (re-apply the geometry when initView()
#   reuses the view) is kept as
#   docs/patches/kylin-virtual-keyboard-preload-rotation.patch -- once the
#   shipped keyboard carries it, build with OSK_ROTATE_ENV=0 and keep
#   OSK_PRELOAD_ENV=1.
#
# The other two keys used by the double-tap feature are runtime state, NOT
# defaults: the gate writes/clears $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/sheng-osk-textactive, and the
# tap daemon only reads it.  animation-enabled is deliberately left at its
# upstream default (true) -- disabling it was measured to change nothing
# (0.31-0.36 s either way), so it is purely cosmetic.
#
# NOTE: install_osk_tap() rewrites the preload-view-enabled line below from
# OSK_PRELOAD_ENV (default: follow OSK_ROTATE_ENV, i.e. true when the rotate
# daemon is installed); this file is the source it installs.

[org.ukui.virtualkeyboard]
preload-view-enabled=true
